## Original Content
<p>In addition to data protection, the EU’s General Data Protection Regulation requires businesses to ensure consumers can exercise their data privacy rights. But first, individuals must know these rights.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://gdpr.eu/consumers-gdpr-data-privacy-rights/">Do consumers know their GDPR data privacy rights?</a> appeared first on <a href="https://gdpr.eu">GDPR.eu</a>.</p>

## Summary
The article discusses GDPR requirements for businesses to enable consumers' data privacy rights. It emphasizes that consumers must first know about these rights to exercise them. The content is sourced from GDPR.eu, focusing on consumer awareness.

## Key Points
- GDPR mandates businesses to ensure consumers can exercise their data privacy rights.
- Consumer awareness of data privacy rights is a prerequisite for exercising them.
- The article highlights the gap between regulatory requirements and consumer knowledge.


